00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:25,580
ends up at waste vegetable oil companies,

732
00:39:25,680 --> 00:39:27,580
who recycle it into various products.

733
00:39:35,200 --> 00:39:38,540
Places like Blue Sky Biofuels in Oakland, California,

734
00:39:38,640 --> 00:39:41,700
are converting this used cooking oil to green energy.

735
00:39:41,701 --> 00:39:44,100
energy.

736
00:39:44,200 --> 00:39:46,200
Blue Sky has been in business for two years.

737
00:39:46,300 --> 00:39:49,440
We actually make clean burning biodiesel out of recycled

738
00:39:49,540 --> 00:39:51,340
cooking oil.

739
00:39:51,440 --> 00:39:54,340
Every year, if the over 3 billion gallons of used

740
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:57,680
cooking oil in the United States became biodiesel, it

741
00:39:57,780 --> 00:40:02,920
would offset about 2 billion gallons of petroleum.

742
00:40:03,020 --> 00:40:05,920
That's enough gas to run every vehicle in the country for

743
00:40:06,020 --> 00:40:09,320
roughly four days.

744
00:40:09,321 --> 00:40:11,660
Blue Sky biofuel trucks collect oil

745
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:15,520
from Northern California sports stadiums, food manufacturers,

746
00:40:15,620 --> 00:40:18,360
and Oakland eateries.

747
00:40:18,460 --> 00:40:20,760
The restaurants have been very supportive.

748
00:40:20,860 --> 00:40:22,800
They're actually, in the past, have been paying

749
00:40:22,900 --> 00:40:24,200
to get rid of their oil.

750
00:40:24,300 --> 00:40:27,540
And right now, with biodiesel, we actually collect for free.

751
00:40:27,640 --> 00:40:29,940
Or in some cases, if they have the right kind of oil,

752
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:34,040
we actually pay them for their oil.

753
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:37,540
Blue Sky has a couple of trucks making the rounds.

754
00:40:37,541 --> 00:40:40,940
Do about 15, 20 stops a day.

755
00:40:41,040 --> 00:40:45,140
Pick up anywhere between 5 to 800 gallons a day.

756
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:52,380
At the biodiesel facility, the driver

757
00:40:52,480 --> 00:40:56,000
pumps out the used cooking oil.

758
00:40:56,100 --> 00:40:59,060
First, various tanks filter and heat the old oil

759
00:40:59,160 --> 00:41:03,700
to remove food scraps, debris, and excess water.

760
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:07,540
This clean oil is now ready to be transformed into biodiesel.

761
00:41:07,541 --> 00:41:09,540
This is the reactor room.

762
00:41:09,541 --> 00:41:11,540
This is actually where we turn the vegetable oil

763
00:41:11,541 --> 00:41:13,540
into biodiesel.

764
00:41:13,541 --> 00:41:16,540
Vegetable oil is too thick to run in a diesel motor

765
00:41:16,541 --> 00:41:17,540
on its own.

766
00:41:17,541 --> 00:41:19,540
So what we do is we actually take the glycerin out

767
00:41:19,541 --> 00:41:22,540
and we replace it with methanol, which is an alcohol,

768
00:41:22,541 --> 00:41:25,540
and actually thins out the vegetable oil.

769
00:41:25,541 --> 00:41:29,540
To do this, Blue Sky introduces a catalyst

770
00:41:29,541 --> 00:41:32,540
to the reactor tank to trigger the process.

771
00:41:32,541 --> 00:41:36,540
In a chemical reaction, the methanol molecules

772
00:41:36,541 --> 00:41:41,040
molecules attached to the fatty acid chain of vegetable oil.

773
00:41:41,140 --> 00:41:43,740
This interaction causes the three bonds of the glycerol

774
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:46,880
molecule to break off, resulting in three long

775
00:41:46,980 --> 00:41:51,180
methyl ester chains, or biodiesel.

776
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:54,000
This biodiesel then travels through a wash tank

777
00:41:54,100 --> 00:41:55,900
to remove any impurities before making it

778
00:41:56,000 --> 00:41:56,900
to the final storage.

779
00:42:00,300 --> 00:42:01,700
So this is the final product.

780
00:42:01,800 --> 00:42:04,540
This is the clean biodiesel ready to go into the diesel

781
00:42:04,640 --> 00:42:05,340
motor.

782
00:42:05,341 --> 00:42:10,140
As you can see, it's crystal clear and ready to be burned.

783
00:42:10,141 --> 00:42:12,140
Besides reducing vehicle emissions,

784
00:42:12,141 --> 00:42:14,940
this clean fuel actually lubricates an engine,

785
00:42:14,941 --> 00:42:17,180
increasing its longevity.

786
00:42:17,181 --> 00:42:20,700
It can also release a rather appetizing smell.

787
00:42:20,701 --> 00:42:24,380
It'll take on the flavors and the smell of the food

788
00:42:24,381 --> 00:42:25,340
that was cooked in it.

789
00:42:25,341 --> 00:42:29,500
So like Thai food oil smells like Thai food.

790
00:42:29,501 --> 00:42:32,940
Blue Sky sends their aromatic 100% biodiesel,

791
00:42:32,941 --> 00:42:36,280
commonly known as B100, to petroleum distributors

792
00:42:36,281 --> 00:42:39,440
and other customers who can use it straight or blend it

793
00:42:39,441 --> 00:42:41,940
with petroleum-based diesel.

794
00:42:41,941 --> 00:42:44,380
Their clients include local business fleets,

795
00:42:44,381 --> 00:42:48,680
Oakland school buses, and the city of San Francisco.

796
00:42:48,681 --> 00:42:52,500
Every single diesel engine, with a few minor exceptions,

797
00:42:52,501 --> 00:42:55,540
in the city of San Francisco of the city's public fleet

798
00:42:55,541 --> 00:42:57,000
is running B20.

799
00:42:57,001 --> 00:43:00,840
The city of San Francisco uses almost 6 million gallons

800
00:43:00,841 --> 00:43:04,540
of fuel a year, which equates to almost a million gallons

801
00:43:04,541 --> 00:43:06,840
of biodiesel that we're consuming,

802
00:43:07,080 --> 00:43:10,040
which is a very large amount of replacement fuel.

803
00:43:11,580 --> 00:43:13,620
The city's Public Utility Commission

804
00:43:13,621 --> 00:43:16,160
is part of a so-called Grease Cycle Program,

805
00:43:16,820 --> 00:43:19,400
which has found ways to use every part of used cooking oil,

806
00:43:19,900 --> 00:43:21,500
even less appetizing bits.

807
00:43:25,440 --> 00:43:27,560
The fuel-ready material goes directly

808
00:43:27,561 --> 00:43:28,860
to the biodiesel manufacturing.

809
00:43:28,861 --> 00:43:31,860
The other material, the food particles,

810
00:43:31,861 --> 00:43:34,360
the kind of the creamy sort of funk,

811
00:43:34,361 --> 00:43:38,360
we actually digest that material.

812
00:43:38,361 --> 00:43:41,360
The bacterial digestion takes place here,

813
00:43:41,361 --> 00:43:45,360
and the end result is methane gas production for energy.

814
00:43:45,361 --> 00:43:47,360
They also have a creative use for the glycerin

815
00:43:47,361 --> 00:43:49,360
that's expelled from biodiesel.

816
00:43:49,361 --> 00:43:52,360
We actually use this glycerin to clean our sewer systems.

817
00:43:52,361 --> 00:43:56,360
So when fats, oils and grease are improperly disposed of

818
00:43:56,361 --> 00:43:59,500
disposed of in the sewer system, they accumulate

819
00:43:59,501 --> 00:44:02,160
on the interior of the pipes and restrict the flow,

820
00:44:02,161 --> 00:44:04,300
much like your arteries and cholesterol.

821
00:44:04,301 --> 00:44:07,920
This glycerin is an ideal way to loosen that material

822
00:44:07,921 --> 00:44:10,800
and discharge it down the system and maintain

823
00:44:10,801 --> 00:44:12,960
the integrity of our sewer system.

824
00:44:12,961 --> 00:44:15,760
I feel almost obligated to order fried food.

825
00:44:15,761 --> 00:44:17,820
That way there's more oil for me to collect

826
00:44:17,821 --> 00:44:21,260
and turn into biodiesel.

827
00:44:21,261 --> 00:44:22,660
Hmm.

828
00:44:22,661 --> 00:44:25,420
Eat fried food and save the planet.

829
00:44:25,421 --> 00:44:26,180
Can't beat that.

